Pydantic v2: `model_validate`, `model_dump`, `model_config = ConfigDict(...)`, `@field_validator`, `@model_validator`, `Field(pattern=...)`, `TypeAdapter(T).validate_python(...)` (not `parse_obj_as`).

===== .claude/rules/forge-python-pytest.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

pytest. Tests assert behaviour: never weaken, remove or skip an assertion to make a test pass.
If an existing test looks wrong, stop and ask; never edit it to make the code pass.

===== .claude/rules/forge-python-sqlalchemy-alembic.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

Alembic with an async engine: `alembic/env.py` runs migrations through `run_async_migrations()` and `connection.run_sync()`. New revisions: `alembic revision --autogenerate -m "<change>"`. Committed revisions are never edited.

===== .claude/rules/forge-python-sqlalchemy.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

SQLAlchemy 2.0 async. Models: `class Base(DeclarativeBase)`, `Mapped[T]`, `mapped_column()`, `relationship(back_populates=...)`. Queries: `select()` with `session.execute()` or `session.scalars()` (`session.query()` is rejected). Sessions: `async_sessionmaker(engine, expire_on_commit=False)`.
Async sessions cannot lazy-load (`MissingGreenlet`): load related rows with `selectinload()`, or declare `lazy="raise"`.
Values reach `text()` SQL as bound parameters (`:id`): an f-string, `.format()`, `%` or `+` inside `text()`, and a string literal passed to `.execute()`, are rejected. Statements that cannot take parameters (`SET`, `SET LOCAL`) may embed a validated value such as an int.

===== .claude/rules/forge-python.md
These are this project's defaults. When the task or the user explicitly asks for something different, do what they ask and point out the conflict; never override an explicit instruction with these defaults.

Python project managed with uv. Tools run from `.venv/bin`. Type checking: basedpyright.
Inside `async def`, the checks reject blocking calls that ruff's ASYNC210, ASYNC230 and ASYNC251 detect (sync HTTP clients, `open()`, `time.sleep`).
Ignore comments name their rule (`# pyright: ignore[ruleName]`), and a changed file may not gain suppression comments.

